; dsv4-lane-band.bml -- the DeepSeek-V4 lane through the model session door on a fixture with a vocabulary: open, ask, N tokens, text, release, equal to the token walk; the refusals, the named endings, the renewal, the plants.
;
; WHAT THIS PINS. The lane is wired (form-cli-model-ds4.fk fcds-lane-wired? 1, model-registry.bml's row deepseek4 dsv4 1) and the session door (form-cli-model-session.fk) takes a DeepSeek-V4 file through the same calls a Qwen
; session is asked through: the admission queue, the seal, the registry's lane gate, the governor's lease, then the arch's seat. The fixture is the real file's tensor types (Q8_0 dense, IQ2_XXS and Q2_K experts: dfx-v-specs) with
; a 32-piece vocabulary Form writes into its header (dfx-vocab-kvs: the markers of the chat template found by their bytes, the letters of the system text and a short prompt, the space piece), so the prompt is tokenized by the
; body's own tokenizer and the chat template, the ids come out of the routed-arena token path and the text goes back through the tokenizer, all on a device. NO REAL FILE IS READ OR MAPPED.
;
; Verdict 4095 when every claim lands:
;   1     the lane is wired and the door admits it: fcds-lane-wired? reads 1 and mr-lane-rows holds EXACTLY the five rows with deepseek4 as (dsv4, 1), the two twins equal; fcms-open-reserved on the sealed fixture answers a LIVE session
;         (reason opened-ds4-driver, a DeepSeek session by shape: the 13-slot context, three state rows), its position the count of the chat template's ids, its capacity that count plus the reserve, a pending id inside the vocabulary
;   2     the flow equals the token walk: fcms-generate of 12 tokens answers ids equal, bit for bit, to the walk the shared token functions give on the same file and prompt (dsv4-open-arena, dsv4-prepare, dsv4-new-state,
;         dsv4-prefill-span-sliced on the template's ids, dsv4-generate), their text is the tokenizer's decode of them, the walk ended max-tokens and the usage line reads the counts, the ending and the last position (the lane adds no behaviour)
;   4     the ledger: while the session is open this process's lease file stands keyed by the file and the residency note names it; after fcms-release-ok? read 1 both are gone, the live Metal handles are what they were, and the
;         held line a refusal prints names the model session and the reason
;   8     the generate door: fcmg-generate-plain-resident (the CLI's `generate` route; its allowance arrives as the plain ledger's query, n is 0) answers the key=value report of the driver (backend, architecture, mode dsv4-native-generate,
;         prompt_tokens, generated_tokens, ending max-tokens, position_limit) with the same text after "text:", keeps no residence, and fcmg-ds4-tokens takes the allowance from whichever of n and query the caller set
;   16    the refusals, word for word: a non-DeepSeek file with a seal reads lane-unwired:unknown: and an unsealed DeepSeek file the seal refusal, each with nothing resident; a DeepSeek file whose header holds a tensor the driver
;         cannot run (attn_kv retyped F16) reads model-driver-gap:<the tensor> before any lease or open; a lease the governor holds back (the injected verdict reserve) reads host-memory-held:reserve with nothing opened and no lease file;
;         a window past the header's context_length, a window no larger than the prompt and an empty prompt refuse typed before any lease; every refusal leaves the live handles as they were
;   32    the position limit and the named endings: a session asked for 3,043 positions is cut to 2,048; walked from position 2,040 for 100 tokens it answers nine ids and ends context-limit, never silently (its usage line reads
;         ending=context-limit position_limit=2047), its next generate answers nothing and keeps the ending; the driver's own indexer rule (dth-pos-ok?) admits 2,047 and refuses 2,048, which is what fcds-indexer-limit says; the one-shot
;         opened for 50 positions ends context-limit at position 49
;   64    the stop id: with the header's eos set to the id the walk makes second, the session answers that one id, ends eos with the stop id pending, the one-shot answers the same ids and eos
;   128   the renewal: fcmr-replace-with-profile-checked on the live session answers changed with the reason fresh-stream-same-weights, a live session at the new prompt's count, the live Metal handles unchanged (the old state released
;         as the second was taken), ids equal to the token walk of the new prompt; a prompt past the window is refused (prompt-context-window-refused) with the session and its state as they were; a second state the governor holds back reads
;         host-memory-held:reserve with the owner unchanged
;   256   the checks can fail: lane flag and registry row that differ are told apart (1/0 and 0/1), a walk that ignores the stop id runs past it, the door's source calls the shared token functions and a copy that enqueues its own
;         layers is told from it (and a whole-stack open is refused), a walk without the position check names the refused step step-refused where the real one names the limit
;   512   the text holds no half character: the bytes of an incomplete UTF-8 tail (a lead byte, a lead with one or two of its continuations) are written \xNN where a bare partial sequence would be a broken string, a whole
;         sequence and an ASCII end are raw bytes, a text that ends on the piece for 0xF0 reads \xf0 (the ids stay the record); the plain render keeps the partial bytes, which is what the rule replaces
;   1024  a renewal's second state the driver refused (nothing) ends by name (new-stream-allocation-refused) and a prefill that stops (an id that is no number) ends by name (new-stream-prefill-refused): the owner is the
;         session it was, the live handles are as they were once the second state is freed and its lease returned, the first stream still walks the token walk's ids and releases; the unguarded count of nothing is a stop
;   2048  the unwind: a step that raises inside the walk answers a session that is not resident, named walk-stopped, with the live handles back at rest, no lease file and no residency note, and its release reads 1; the
;         same walk without the unwind raises with the handles and the lease still held (they are given back after, by the release)
;
; REQUIRES: a live Metal device -- needs one behind the handle door; plain fkwu reads 0. The memory governor must read room for the session's private margin (8 GiB) twice; the band takes real leases and gives them back. Light GPU: the
; 1.7 MB fixtures, a few hundred positions. Writes only under temp_dir (the fixtures, their seals and the seal's verified note) and removes what it made; the model admission queue's note for the fixture path is dropped by the release.
// preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk form-stdlib/str-byte-at.fk form-stdlib/equireach.fk form-stdlib/gguf-manifest.fk form-stdlib/dsv4-fixture-gguf.fk form-stdlib/dsv4-layout.fk native/metal/dsv4-bind.fk form-stdlib/dsv4-kernels.fk native/metal/dsv4-open.fk native/metal/dsv4-layer.fk native/metal/dsv4-token-handle.fk form-stdlib/dsv4-compressor.fk form-stdlib/f16-decode.fk form-stdlib/dsv4-lease.fk form-stdlib/dsv4-tokenizer.fk form-stdlib/bml/memory-governor.bml form-stdlib/form-cli-model-ds4.fk form-stdlib/model-registry.bml form-stdlib/form-cli-model-session.fk form-stdlib/bml/form-cli-model-renew.bml form-stdlib/bml/dsv4-session-ask.bml form-stdlib/qwen35-artifact-seal-reader.fk
section [form.bml] {
 class Dsv4Lane {
  def dlb-bit(held, bit) = held ? bit : 0;
  def dlb-has?(s, part) = str_find(s, part, 0) >= 0;
  // ---- the fixture's vocabulary: the template's markers (the file's own bytes), the system text's letters and a prompt's, the space piece -----------------------------
  def dlb-tokens() = ["<｜begin▁of▁sentence｜>", "<｜end▁of▁sentence｜>", "<｜User｜>", "<｜Assistant｜>", "<think>", "</think>", "Y", "o", "u", "Ġ", "a", "r", "e", "h", "l", "p", "f", "s", "i", "t", "n", "b", "c", "d", "g", "m", "w", "y", ".", ",", "?", "ð"];
  // id 31 is the piece for the byte 0xF0 (the lead of a four-byte character): a text that ends on it ends mid-character
  def dlb-lead-id() = 31;
  def dlb-vocab(eos) = dfx-vocab-kvs(dlb-tokens(), [], 0, eos);
  def dlb-prompt() = "the cat is a";
  def dlb-prompt2() = "a hat is a";
  def dlb-n() = 12;
  // a fixture with a tensor the driver has no kernel for: a Q8_0 projection retyped F16 (the layout's gap list names it)
  def dlb-retype(specs, name, ty) = len(specs) == 0 ? [] : cons(specs[0][0] == name ? [specs[0][0], ty, specs[0][2], specs[0][3], specs[0][4], specs[0][5]] : specs[0], dlb-retype(specs[1:], name, ty));
  def dlb-gap-specs() = dlb-retype(dfx-v-specs(), "blk.0.attn_kv.weight", 1);
  // the seal as the fetch organ writes it: the size and the SHA-256 of the file
  def dlb-seal(path) = write_file_text(qaf-seal-path-for(path), "qaf-seal1:" ++ int_to_str(file_size(path)) ++ ":" ++ qaf-string-hex(saj-file-digest(path, file_size(path))));
  def dlb-unseal(path) = host_path_remove(qaf-seal-path-for(path)) + host_path_remove(qaf-verified-path-for(path));
  def dlb-lease-path() = mg-lease-path(mg-lease-dir(), host_pid());
  def dlb-lease-held?() = file_size(dlb-lease-path()) > 0;
  def dlb-lease-keyed?(path) = dlb-has?(read_file(dlb-lease-path()) ?? "", path);
  def dlb-noted?(path) = len(filter(line => trim(line) == path, adm-note-lines(adm-root(), host_pid()))) > 0;
  // ---- the token walk the lane must equal: the shared functions, no door ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  def dlb-walk(path, ids, cap, n, stops) {
   let ctx = dsv4-open-arena(path, cap, 1, dls-cache-experts());
   let prepared = len(ctx) == 13 ? dsv4-prepare(ctx) : 0;
   let sts = prepared == 1 ? dsv4-new-state(ctx[2], ctx[0], cap) : nothing();
   let pf = nothing?(sts) ? nothing() : dsv4-prefill-span-sliced(ctx, sts, ids, 0);
   let more = nothing?(pf) ? [] : dsv4-generate(ctx, sts, pf[0], pf[1], n - 1, stops, []);
   let left = len(ctx) == 13 ? dsv4-close(ctx, nothing?(sts) ? [] : sts) : [];
   nothing?(pf) ? [] : (len(stops) > 0 && pf[0] == stops[0] ? [] : cons(pf[0], more));
  }
  // the first id the walk makes that no earlier one was: the stop id the eos fixture names
  def dlb-novel(ids, k) = k >= len(ids) ? 0 - 1 : (dlb-seen?(ids[k], ids[0:k]) ? dlb-novel(ids, k + 1) : k);
  def dlb-seen?(x, xs) = len(xs) == 0 ? false : (xs[0] == x || dlb-seen?(x, xs[1:]));
  // ---- the plants ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  def dlb-twin?(flag, row) = flag == row;
  // the door's source calls the shared token functions (the arena open, prepare, state, prefill, decode, close) and none of the layer-level or whole-stack ones
  def dlb-shared-calls?(src) = dlb-has?(src, "dsv4-open-arena(") && dlb-has?(src, "dsv4-prepare(") && dlb-has?(src, "dsv4-new-state(") && dlb-has?(src, "dsv4-prefill-span-sliced(") && dlb-has?(src, "dsv4-decode(") && dlb-has?(src, "dsv4-close(")
   && !dlb-has?(src, "dth-stage(") && !dlb-has?(src, "dsv4-forward-state(") && !dlb-has?(src, "metal_enqueue(") && !dlb-has?(src, "dkr-go(") && !dlb-has?(src, "dxa-open(") && !dlb-has?(src, "dsv4-open-span(");
  // fcds-gen without its position check: the driver's refusal at the limit reads as a refused step
  def dlb-gen-nolimit(ctx, sts, id, pos, n, stops, acc) = n <= 0 ? [acc, "max-tokens"] : fcds-gen-step(ctx, sts, id, pos, n, stops, acc, dsv4-decode(ctx, sts, id, pos));
  def dlb-held() = (who, key, shared, priv) => [0, "reserve", 100, 50, 1000, 0, 0];
  def dlb-live-held?(s) = fcms-live?(s) == 1 && fcms-resident?(s) == 1;
  // a step that raises (a stop inside the walk), and a prefill that raises (an id that is no number)
  def dlb-raising-step() = (s, id, pos) => form_error("planted decode stop");
  // the render without the incomplete-tail rule: what the text was before
  def dlb-plain-render(bs) = tkz-render-acc(bs, "");
  // the count of the second state's handles as the discard asked it before it knew nothing: a stop on nothing
  def dlb-bare-count(sts) = len(dsv4-state-handles(sts));
 }
 let root = temp_dir() ++ "/dsv4-lane-band-" ++ now_unix_ms().str();
 let pathA = root ++ "-a.gguf";
 let pathB = root ++ "-b.gguf";
 let pathG = root ++ "-gap.gguf";
 let pathU = root ++ "-unsealed.gguf";
 let pathT = root ++ "-text.txt";
 let wroteA = dfx-write-with(pathA, dfx-v-specs(), dlb-vocab(1));
 let sealedA = dlb-seal(pathA);
 let wroteG = dfx-write-with(pathG, dlb-gap-specs(), dlb-vocab(1));
 let sealedG = dlb-seal(pathG);
 let wroteU = dfx-write-with(pathU, dfx-v-specs(), dlb-vocab(1));
 let wroteT = write_file(pathT, "this is not a model, it is a line of text kept to prove the lane gate names the architecture it finds");
 let sealedT = dlb-seal(pathT);
 let live0 = dvb-live();
 let mapped0 = dvb-mapped();
 let srcA = tkz-src(pathA);
 let idsA = fcds-prompt-ids(srcA, dlb-prompt());
 let said0 = print_str("fixture " ++ wroteA.str() ++ " B, vocabulary " ++ tkz-vocab-n(srcA).str() ++ ", the prompt's " ++ len(idsA).str() ++ " template ids " ++ idsA.str());
 // 1, 2, 4: the flow through the session door
 let s1 = fcms-open-reserved(pathA, dlb-prompt(), dlb-n(), "full");
 let leaseDuring = dlb-lease-held?();
 let keyedDuring = dlb-lease-keyed?(pathA);
 let notedDuring = dlb-noted?(pathA);
 let said1 = print_str("session: status " ++ (String) fcms-status(s1) ++ " reason " ++ (String) fcms-reason(s1) ++ " pos " ++ fcms-pos(s1).str() ++ " maxpos " ++ fcms-maxpos(s1).str() ++ " pending " ++ fcms-pending(s1).str() ++ " lease " ++ leaseDuring.str() ++ " noted " ++ notedDuring.str());
 let r1 = try fcds-lane-wired?() == 1 && (Value) mr-lane-rows() == [["qwen35", "q38", 1], ["qwen35moe", "qsx", 0], ["llama", "dth", 0], ["qwen4exp", "q4t", 0], ["deepseek4", "dsv4", 1]] && mr-lane-for("deepseek4") == fcds-lane-name() && mr-wired?("deepseek4") == fcds-lane-wired?()
  && fcds-lane-route("deepseek4") == "deepseek4" && fcds-lane-route("qwen35") == "qwen35" && fcms-live?(s1) == 1 && (String) fcms-reason(s1) == "opened-ds4-driver" && fcms-ds4?(s1) && len(fcms-ctx(s1)) == 13 && len(fcms-sts(s1)) == 3
  && fcms-pos(s1) == len(idsA) && len(idsA) > 0 && fcms-maxpos(s1) == len(idsA) + dlb-n() && fcms-prompt-ids(s1) == len(idsA) && fcms-pending(s1) >= 0 && fcms-pending(s1) < 32 catch false;
 let g1 = fcms-generate(s1, dlb-n());
 let ids1 = fcms-generation-ids(g1);
 let text1 = fcms-generation-text(g1);
 let s1b = fcms-generation-session(g1);
 let usage1 = fcms-usage-line-ds4(s1b);
 let said2 = print_str("generated " ++ ids1.str() ++ " text [" ++ text1 ++ "] ending " ++ (String) fcms-ending(s1b) ++ " | " ++ usage1);
 // 128 (first half): the renewal on the live session, before it is released
 let liveBeforeRenew = dvb-live();
 let ren = fcmr-replace-with-profile-checked(s1b, dlb-prompt2(), "full", fcmr-any-prompt, 0);
 let s1c = fcmr-session(ren);
 let liveAfterRenew = dvb-live();
 let ids2src = fcds-prompt-ids(srcA, dlb-prompt2());
 let g2 = fcms-live?(s1c) == 1 ? fcms-generate(s1c, dlb-n()) : fcms-generation("", [], s1c);
 let ids2 = fcms-generation-ids(g2);
 let s1d = fcms-generation-session(g2);
 let said3 = print_str("renewal: changed " ++ fcmr-changed(ren).str() ++ " reason " ++ (String) fcmr-reason(ren) ++ " pos " ++ fcms-pos(s1c).str() ++ " live " ++ liveBeforeRenew.str() ++ "/" ++ liveAfterRenew.str() ++ " ids " ++ ids2.str());
 let tooLong = fcmr-replace-with-profile-checked(s1d, "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa", "full", fcmr-any-prompt, 0);
 let liveAfterLong = dvb-live();
 let heldRenew = fcmr-granted("dsv4-lane-band", s1d, ids2src, fcmr-reading("dsv4-lane-band", "independent-stream-needed", 0, json-node-string("fresh conversation state"), json-node-string("existing conversation state")), [0, "reserve", 100, 50, 1000, 0, 0]);
 let liveAfterHeld = dvb-live();
 let said4 = print_str("renewal refusals: too long " ++ (String) fcmr-reason(tooLong) ++ " held " ++ (String) fcmr-reason(heldRenew));
 let rel1 = fcms-release-ok?(s1d);
 let leaseAfter = dlb-lease-held?();
 let notedAfter = dlb-noted?(pathA);
 let liveAfter1 = dvb-live();
 // the token walks the lane must equal (on the shared functions; each opens and closes its own context)
 let walkA = dlb-walk(pathA, idsA, len(idsA) + dlb-n(), dlb-n(), fcds-stops(srcA));
 let walkA2 = dlb-walk(pathA, ids2src, len(idsA) + dlb-n(), dlb-n(), fcds-stops(srcA));
 let said5 = print_str("token walks " ++ walkA.str() ++ " | " ++ walkA2.str());
 let r2 = try len(ids1) == dlb-n() && ids1 == walkA && (String) text1 == (String) fcds-text(srcA, ids1) && len(text1) > 0 && (String) fcms-ending(s1b) == "max-tokens"
  && (String) usage1 == ("usage: prompt_tokens=" ++ len(idsA).str() ++ " generated_tokens=" ++ dlb-n().str() ++ " ending=max-tokens position=" ++ (len(idsA) + dlb-n() - 2).str() ++ " capacity=" ++ (len(idsA) + dlb-n()).str() ++ " position_limit=2047") catch false;
 let r4 = try leaseDuring && keyedDuring && notedDuring && rel1 == 1 && !leaseAfter && !notedAfter && liveAfter1 == live0
  && dlb-has?(mg-line("model session " ++ pathA, 0, [0, "reserve", 100, 50, 1000, 0, 0]), "[memory] held model session") && dlb-has?(mg-line("model session " ++ pathA, 0, [0, "reserve", 100, 50, 1000, 0, 0]), "reserve") catch false;
 let r128 = try fcmr-changed(ren) == 1 && (String) fcmr-reason(ren) == "fresh-stream-same-weights" && fcms-live?(s1c) == 1 && fcms-pos(s1c) == len(ids2src) && len(ids2src) > 0 && liveAfterRenew == liveBeforeRenew && ids2 == walkA2 && len(ids2) == dlb-n()
  && fcmr-changed(tooLong) == 0 && (String) fcmr-reason(tooLong) == "prompt-context-window-refused" && liveAfterLong == liveAfterRenew && fcms-live?(fcmr-session(tooLong)) == 1
  && fcmr-changed(heldRenew) == 0 && (String) fcmr-reason(heldRenew) == "host-memory-held:reserve" && liveAfterHeld == liveAfterLong catch false;
 // 8: the generate door (the CLI's `generate` route: the allowance is the plain ledger's query)
 let gen = fcmg-generate-plain-resident(fcmr-none(), pathA, dlb-prompt(), dlb-n());
 let report = gen[0];
 let liveAfterGen = dvb-live();
 let leaseAfterGen = dlb-lease-held?();
 let said6 = print_str("report:\n" ++ report ++ "\n");
 let r8 = try dlb-has?(report, "backend=form-native-metal-dsv4-driver") && dlb-has?(report, "architecture=deepseek4") && dlb-has?(report, "mode=dsv4-native-generate") && dlb-has?(report, "prompt_tokens=" ++ len(idsA).str() ++ "\n")
  && dlb-has?(report, "generated_tokens=" ++ dlb-n().str() ++ "\n") && dlb-has?(report, "ending=max-tokens\n") && dlb-has?(report, "capacity=" ++ (len(idsA) + dlb-n() + 1).str() ++ "\n") && dlb-has?(report, "position_limit=2047\n") && dlb-has?(report, "text:\n" ++ text1) && fcmr-live?(gen[1]) == 0
  && liveAfterGen == live0 && !leaseAfterGen && fcmg-ds4-tokens(0, 24) == 24 && fcmg-ds4-tokens(5, 0) == 5 && fcmg-ds4-tokens(5, 24) == 5 catch false;
 // 16: the refusals
 let liveR0 = dvb-live();
 let textOpen = fcms-open(pathT, dlb-prompt(), 64);
 let unsealedOpen = fcms-open(pathU, dlb-prompt(), 64);
 let gapOpen = fcms-open(pathG, dlb-prompt(), 64);
 let leaseAfterGap = dlb-lease-held?();
 let heldParts = fcds-open-parts-with(dlb-held(), pathA, srcA, dlb-prompt(), 0, dlb-n());
 let leaseAfterHeldOpen = dlb-lease-held?();
 let pastContext = fcds-open-parts(pathA, srcA, dlb-prompt(), 70000, 0);
 let tooSmall = fcds-open-parts(pathA, srcA, dlb-prompt(), len(idsA), 0);
 let emptyPrompt = fcds-open-parts(pathA, srcA, "", 64, 0);
 let leaseAfterTyped = dlb-lease-held?();
 let liveR1 = dvb-live();
 let said7 = print_str("refusals: text [" ++ (String) fcms-reason(textOpen) ++ "] unsealed [" ++ (String) fcms-reason(unsealedOpen) ++ "] gap [" ++ (String) fcms-reason(gapOpen) ++ "] held [" ++ (String) heldParts[1] ++ "] context [" ++ (String) pastContext[1] ++ "] small [" ++ (String) tooSmall[1] ++ "] empty [" ++ (String) emptyPrompt[1] ++ "]");
 let r16 = try fcms-live?(textOpen) == 0 && fcms-resident?(textOpen) == 0 && (String) fcms-reason(textOpen) == "lane-unwired:unknown:" && fcms-live?(unsealedOpen) == 0 && fcms-resident?(unsealedOpen) == 0
  && dlb-has?(fcms-reason(unsealedOpen), "no current Form-native SHA-256 seal") && fcms-live?(gapOpen) == 0 && fcms-resident?(gapOpen) == 0 && dlb-has?(fcms-reason(gapOpen), "model-driver-gap:") && dlb-has?(fcms-reason(gapOpen), "attn_kv.weight type 1") && !leaseAfterGap
  && (String) heldParts[0] == "nothing" && (String) heldParts[1] == "host-memory-held:reserve" && len(heldParts[2]) == 0 && !leaseAfterHeldOpen && mg-memory-held?(heldParts[1])
  && (String) pastContext[1] == "session-context-window-refused" && (String) tooSmall[1] == "session-context-window-refused" && (String) emptyPrompt[1] == "initial-turn-encoded-no-ids" && !leaseAfterTyped && liveR1 == liveR0 catch false;
 // 32: the position limit and the named endings
 let s2 = fcms-open-reserved(pathA, dlb-prompt(), 3000, "full");
 let ctx2 = fcms-ctx(s2);
 let s2b = fcms-with-stream(s2, 2040, fcms-pending(s2), 0, fcms-generated-ids(s2), fcms-injected-ids(s2), fcms-observations(s2));
 let g3 = fcms-generate(s2b, 100);
 let ids3 = fcms-generation-ids(g3);
 let s2c = fcms-generation-session(g3);
 let usage3 = fcms-usage-line-ds4(s2c);
 let g4 = fcms-generate(s2c, 5);
 let s2d = fcms-generation-session(g4);
 let pinOk = len(ctx2) == 13 && dth-pos-ok?(ctx2, 0, fcds-indexer-limit() - 1) && !dth-pos-ok?(ctx2, 0, fcds-indexer-limit()) && fcds-indexer-limit() == 2048;
 let said8 = print_str("limit: maxpos " ++ fcms-maxpos(s2).str() ++ " ids " ++ len(ids3).str() ++ " ending " ++ (String) fcms-ending(s2c) ++ " pos " ++ fcms-pos(s2c).str() ++ " | " ++ usage3 ++ " | again " ++ len(fcms-generation-ids(g4)).str() ++ " [" ++ (String) fcms-ending(s2d) ++ "]");
 // the plant: the same step past the limit without the position check (asked of the ended session's context, a fresh state)
 let nolimitSts = len(ctx2) == 13 ? dsv4-new-state(ctx2[2], ctx2[0], dso-cap(ctx2)) : nothing();
 let realEnd = nothing?(nolimitSts) ? [] : fcds-gen(ctx2, nolimitSts, 5, 2048, 4, [], []);
 let plantEnd = nothing?(nolimitSts) ? [] : dlb-gen-nolimit(ctx2, nolimitSts, 5, 2048, 4, [], []);
 let nolimitFreed = nothing?(nolimitSts) ? [] : dsv4-free-state(nolimitSts);
 let rel2 = fcms-release-ok?(s2d);
 let liveAfter2 = dvb-live();
 let runSrc = tkz-src(pathA);
 let runCalled = record_new(0, "n", 0);
 let shortRun = fcds-run-open(pathA, runSrc, idsA, 100, 50, () => record_set(runCalled, "n", record_get(runCalled, "n") + 1));
